    <sectiondef kind="private-static-func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge_1a9b58ab4d1363eeb86bdbc447816d8ba5" prot="private" static="yes" nodiscard="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::unique_ptr&lt; <ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge_1ada8a6b69e531577f2c5a0818ddb142a7" kindref="member">TensorMmapBridge</ref> &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::unique_ptr&lt; TensorMmapBridge &gt; themis::tensor::TensorMmapBridge::buildFromTrain</definition>
        <argsstring>(const storage::TTTrain &amp;train)</argsstring>
        <name>buildFromTrain</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::tensor::TensorMmapBridge::buildFromTrain</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const storage::TTTrain &amp;</type>
          <declname>train</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Build a bridge from a TTTrain using MAP_ANONYMOUS + memcpy. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Page-pins each TT-core array in an anonymous mmap region so that the GGML bridge can reference data pointers without holding the index lock. When an SST-map function is injected via <ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge_1a306df8265797f185df6b40be00e45bba" kindref="member">setSstMapFn()</ref>, the zero-copy MAP_SHARED path is used for any core for which the function returns a non-null pointer.</para>
<para>PERMANENT FALLBACK NOTE: This is the always-available fallback path. For zero-copy MAP_SHARED over real SST file pages, inject a <ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge_1ad72a420bd8d2635b98b75add7c503514" kindref="member">SstMapFn</ref> via <ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge_1a306df8265797f185df6b40be00e45bba" kindref="member">setSstMapFn()</ref> or use buildFromFd() when a backing file descriptor is available. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/tensor/tensor_mmap_bridge.h" line="143" column="5" bodyfile="src/tensor/tensor_mmap_bridge.cpp" bodystart="146" bodyend="224"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge_1acf5522d67af459527a16a1537d91a252" prot="private" static="yes" nodiscard="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::unique_ptr&lt; <ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge_1ada8a6b69e531577f2c5a0818ddb142a7" kindref="member">TensorMmapBridge</ref> &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::unique_ptr&lt; TensorMmapBridge &gt; themis::tensor::TensorMmapBridge::buildFromFd</definition>
        <argsstring>(const storage::TTTrain &amp;train, int fd, std::size_t byte_offset=0)</argsstring>
        <name>buildFromFd</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::tensor::TensorMmapBridge::buildFromFd</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const storage::TTTrain &amp;</type>
          <declname>train</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>fd</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>std::size_t</type>
          <declname>byte_offset</declname>
          <defval>0</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Build a bridge using MAP_SHARED on a backing file descriptor. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When <computeroutput>fd</computeroutput> is a valid open file descriptor (≥ 0) and the platform supports mmap(MAP_SHARED), each TT-core region is mapped directly from the file at the given <computeroutput>byte_offset</computeroutput> without any memcpy. This is the production zero-copy path for SST-resident TT-trains.</para>
<para>Ownership: the caller retains ownership of <computeroutput>fd</computeroutput>; the bridge does not close it. Regions mapped with MAP_SHARED are tracked as <computeroutput>externally_owned = true</computeroutput> (the destructor calls munmap but NOT close).</para>
<para>PERMANENT FALLBACK NOTE: When <computeroutput>fd</computeroutput> &lt; 0, or when the platform does not support mmap(MAP_SHARED), the call transparently falls back to buildFromTrain(train) (MAP_ANONYMOUS<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>memcpy).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>train</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Decomposed TT-train whose float data populates the map. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fd</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Open read-only file descriptor for the backing SST file. Pass -1 to always use the MAP_ANONYMOUS fallback. </para>
</parameterdescription>
